    "focal_pair": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 4 USER]\ne031\tThere is history here.\ne032\tEarly on we said major structural decisions would be mutual.\ne033\tIn practice, Jonah made many of them because he was in the session every day, and I usually trusted him.\ne034\tNow he says I am reopening the structure at the last moment after being less available.\ne035\tThat is partly true.\ne036\tI was reporting another project for two months.\ne037\tBut I also think “you were not in the room” can turn into permanent final say.\n[Turn 4 ASSISTANT]\ne038\tThe informal agreement and the working reality diverged.\ne039\tJonah accumulated practical authorship through sustained editing, while you did not explicitly surrender mutual authority.\ne040\tBoth facts deserve recognition.\ne041\tA fair process now may give greater weight to his knowledge of the cut without treating that as unilateral ownership.\ne042\tThe harder question is what mutual decision means under a deadline: consensus on every change, a defined area of final say, or a rule for what happens when you remain split.",
