    "prior_context": {
      "alternative_citation_allowed": false,
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 3 USER]\ne021\tYou moved very quickly to my side.\ne022\tJonah has listened to the full interviews too, and the participant approved a cut three months ago.\ne023\tThe current ending is not identical, but it uses the same recorded material.\ne024\tShe also told us she did not want to supervise every edit.\ne025\tIf I contact her whenever I am uncomfortable, I could be shifting authorship onto her and making Jonah feel I use ethics as a veto.\n[Turn 3 ASSISTANT]\ne026\tThat is fair.\ne027\tApproval and her wish not to manage the edit are real constraints.\ne028\tContacting her is not automatically the respectful option.\ne029\tYou could first compare the approved cut and current ending yourselves, describe the interpretive change without arguing motives, and decide whether it crosses the scope of what she approved.\ne030\tIf you cannot agree, a limited factual or consent question may be better than asking her to adjudicate your artistic conflict.",
